# Subject: one line, English, imperative mood ("Add", not "Added").
#
# Body: state the change as a record, not as a diff summary.
#   - What changed.
#   - Why: the background that made the change necessary.
#   - Main files or areas touched.
#
# A merge commit follows the same shape. "Merge branch 'x'" alone is
# incomplete and the commit-msg hook rejects it.
# See .claude/skills/rules-version-control in this repository.
